(A) The declared world slits_matter: S = 1, the family `matter` of content M = 64 units per row, so E'_0 = Q S M = 4096;
    the action h = 1024, the momentum p = 220 label units along each fan direction (the same |p| on every row of a record).
  W = 16922416, E' = isqrt(W) = 4113 (4113^2 = 16916769 <= W < 16924996); gamma = E' / E'_0 = 4113/4096 = 1.00415
  the pace p / E' = 220/4113 = 0.05349 Links per interval = 0.0926 c; the photon's 32 / 55 = 0.5818
  de Broglie: the turn per Link |p| N / h = 55/4 steps (by_drive(acc, 14080, 1024) per Link), lambda = h / |p| = 256/55 = 4.6545 Links (the photon world's 4.654)
  the small-momentum expansion: E' - E'_0 = 17 against 3 p^2 / (2 E'_0) = 9075/512 = 17.72; the next term -9 p^4 / (8 E'_0^3) = -0.0383
  the dispersion's grain: E'^2 <= W < (E' + 1)^2, so the pace |p| / E' is within a part in E' of |p| / sqrt W: a part in 4113 here

(B) The two-path law of 7.1 with lambda = h / |p| (slits_low's geometry: s = 10, D = 44, the screen's fan by angle):
  the bright fringe j = 1 at |y| = 23.3 about the centre, the pixels 36.7 and 83.3 (7.1 at the photon's lambda: 23.3, the pixels 36.7 and 83.3)
  the paraxial spacing lambda D / s = 20.5 pixels (not the check: y / D is 0.5 at the first fringe)

(C) The arrival: the flight time L / v for the centre pixel and the edge of the first fringe:
  the centre: the paths 44.28 and 44.28 Links, the arrivals 828 and 828 intervals after the birth (the photon's 76 and 76)
  the first fringe: the paths 52.32 and 47.65 Links, the arrivals 978 and 891 intervals after the birth (the photon's 90 and 82)

(D) The confrontation's numbers (dimensionless): Jonsson 1961 (50 keV electrons, the slits 0.3 micrometre wide, 1 micrometre apart):
  lambda = h c / (p c) with p c = sqrt(2 m c^2 E (1 + E / (2 m c^2))) = 231516.5 eV: lambda = 5.355 pm; lambda / s = 5.36e-6 (the law's world: 0.465)
  Tonomura 1989: 50 kV electrons through an electron biprism, the pattern built one electron at a time (the law's wheel, one click per birth).
